WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:03.601
-Welcome back. Ben Stiller is joining us right now.

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:05.601
Ah, we love you.

00:00:05.601 --> 00:00:07.601
Ben, I want to talk about your new show,

00:00:07.601 --> 00:00:08.734
your new series, "Severance."

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:10.901
It's on Apple TV+.

00:00:10.901 --> 00:00:12.667
I love it. It's getting great reviews.

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:13.868
Congrats, by the way. -Thanks, man.

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:17.434
-Adam Scott, who I love as well.

00:00:17.434 --> 00:00:19.701
It's a trippy concept.

00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:21.634
-Yeah, I'm not in it.

00:00:21.634 --> 00:00:23.767
I directed it with another director.

00:00:23.767 --> 00:00:25.501
Aoife McArdle, a great director, and produced.

00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:28.601
But it's Adam Scott starring with Patricia Arquette

00:00:28.601 --> 00:00:30.868
and John Turturro, Chris Walken.

00:00:30.868 --> 00:00:32.901
A great cast.

00:00:32.901 --> 00:00:35.234
But he plays the guy who works at a company where you get

00:00:35.234 --> 00:00:36.901
a chip implanted in your head.

00:00:36.901 --> 00:00:39.267
And when you go to work, you go in the elevator,

00:00:39.267 --> 00:00:40.434
and the trip gets triggered.

00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:42.834
And you don't remember anything about your life

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:44.000
when you go down to work.

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:45.367
And then, you do your work day,

00:00:45.367 --> 00:00:46.601
and then, at work, you leave,

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:48.033
and the chip gets triggered again,

00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:50.701
and you don't remember anything that happened at work.

00:00:50.701 --> 00:00:51.767
So, it's --

00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:53.400
-Yeah, so, it's a trippy thing.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:55.767
-It's not really sci-fi, but it's like

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:58.200
a weird alternate reality.

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:01.701
Yeah, which was also kind of, you know --

00:01:01.701 --> 00:01:04.133
working on it in our own alternate reality

00:01:04.133 --> 00:01:05.834
we've all been living in -- -With COVID.

00:01:05.834 --> 00:01:07.367
-The last couple of years has been interesting.

00:01:07.367 --> 00:01:09.000
-It must have been trippy doing that.

00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:11.934
-Yeah, because we ended up shooting for a long time.

00:01:11.934 --> 00:01:15.467
And it has been really hard to do stuff --

00:01:15.467 --> 00:01:18.667
to make productions -- just in terms

00:01:18.667 --> 00:01:20.467
of all the protocols and everything.

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:22.067
And the show take place in this

00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:25.234
sort of weird maze-like environment

00:01:25.234 --> 00:01:27.767
of these white, nondescript halls that are below

00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:29.901
The main buildings where everybody works.

00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:32.501
So we would go to work in the sound stage.

00:01:32.501 --> 00:01:34.133
And you'd get to the sound stage,

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:37.434
and then you'd have to walk down these long, white,

00:01:37.434 --> 00:01:39.934
maze-like halls to get to the sound stage

00:01:39.934 --> 00:01:43.467
that was long, white maze-like halls.

00:01:43.467 --> 00:01:45.000
-Yeah. -Yeah.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:47.300
And then waiting for you when you got all the way to the end

00:01:47.300 --> 00:01:50.567
of the long maze hall was John Turturro and Chris Walken

00:01:50.567 --> 00:01:52.901
with surgical gloves and masks.

00:01:52.901 --> 00:01:56.367
Which was actually a nightmare I had as a teenager.

00:01:56.367 --> 00:02:00.834
It was definitely challenging, but it was also --

00:02:00.834 --> 00:02:03.701
It kind of I think contributed to the vibe of the show, also.

00:02:03.701 --> 00:02:05.033
-It's fantastic.

00:02:05.033 --> 00:02:07.167
It's so well-directed and so well done and well-lit.

00:02:07.167 --> 00:02:08.834
But those hallways, like you're saying.

00:02:08.834 --> 00:02:10.868
There's one scene where you don't really know

00:02:10.868 --> 00:02:13.601
what's happening that first 20 minutes of the first episode.

00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:15.934
In 10 minutes, I go, "What is happening? I'm into this."

00:02:15.934 --> 00:02:18.400
I'm so -- I'm like -- And then --

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.367
Who -- There's a new actress. I don't really...

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:22.567
-Britt Lower, who plays Helly. -Oh, my gosh.

00:02:22.567 --> 00:02:23.901
-Yeah. Yeah.

00:02:23.901 --> 00:02:25.200
-She's unbelievable. -Yeah, she's great.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.234
-And so it starts with her, and you go, "Okay."

00:02:27.234 --> 00:02:29.000
And then they're going down this hallway,

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.200
and the hallway doesn't really end.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:32.667
-Right. Right. -And then eventually it does.

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:35.400
-She realizes she can't leave. She's the new employee.

00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:37.968
So, yeah, it's a little bit nightmarish.

00:02:37.968 --> 00:02:40.634
But, you know, it was also really interesting

00:02:40.634 --> 00:02:43.801
working with these consults because the actors

00:02:43.801 --> 00:02:45.267
are at these workstations

00:02:45.267 --> 00:02:47.901
and their characters don't know what they're actually doing.

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:49.968
So -- But the workstations actually work.

00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:51.934
So, we had these numbers on the workstations

00:02:51.934 --> 00:02:53.868
that they could then... -You could click and drag.

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:55.167
-They could click and drag.

00:02:55.167 --> 00:02:56.934
-I tried to figure it out, too. -Yeah, yeah.

00:02:56.934 --> 00:02:58.334
They got really good at doing it,

00:02:58.334 --> 00:02:59.634
thought they had no idea what they were doing.

00:02:59.634 --> 00:03:01.367
-And it really isn't doing anything.

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:02.801
We don't know. -Yeah. Exactly. We don't know.

00:03:02.801 --> 00:03:04.133
-We don't know. How many episodes are there?

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:05.934
-Nine episodes for the first season.

00:03:05.934 --> 00:03:08.167
-There's two out right now. They're both awesome.

00:03:08.167 --> 00:03:10.567
I just finished the second one yesterday.

00:03:10.567 --> 00:03:12.133
Every Friday they come out, right?

00:03:12.133 --> 00:03:13.501
-Yeah, yeah. -On Apple TV Plus.

00:03:13.501 --> 00:03:15.167
-And you gotta check it out. It is awesome.

00:03:15.167 --> 00:03:18.667
-Can I just say, congrats, man on that movie?

00:03:18.667 --> 00:03:19.901
It's so amazing. -Of course, of course.

00:03:19.901 --> 00:03:21.767
-Thank you. -So amazing.

00:03:21.767 --> 00:03:24.234
-[ Cheers and applause ] -As a -- Yeah.

00:03:24.234 --> 00:03:25.834
I worship you as a drummer and a musician

00:03:25.834 --> 00:03:27.267
but also now as a filmmaker.

00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:29.734
And I grew up in New York, so, like, just to have

00:03:29.734 --> 00:03:32.501
that experience of seeing that whole event that happened,

00:03:32.501 --> 00:03:34.100
not knowing anything about it,

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:36.467
and the emotionality of that movie was just beautiful.

00:03:36.467 --> 00:03:37.767
So congrats, man.

00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:40.834
-That's awesome. That's how you do it right there.

00:03:40.834 --> 00:03:42.434
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:03:42.434 --> 00:03:44.434
Here's a look at the first episode of "Severance."

00:03:44.434 --> 00:03:45.934
Check this out.

00:03:45.934 --> 00:03:48.901
[ Keyboard clacking, computer beeping ]

00:03:48.901 --> 00:03:50.767
-So I'll never leave here?

00:03:52.734 --> 00:03:54.534
-You'll leave at 5:00.

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:57.934
Well, actually, they stagger exits, so 5:15.

00:03:57.934 --> 00:03:59.901
-Hm. -But it won't feel like it,

00:03:59.901 --> 00:04:02.534
not to this version of you, anyway.

00:04:03.934 --> 00:04:06.067
-Do I have a family?

00:04:06.067 --> 00:04:07.567
-You never know.

00:04:09.267 --> 00:04:11.901
-And I have no choice.

00:04:11.901 --> 00:04:14.767
-Well, every time you find yourself here,

00:04:14.767 --> 00:04:17.367
it's because you chose to come back.

00:04:21.367 --> 00:04:22.801
-[ Scoffs ]

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:27.767
-Ben Stiller, everyone, right there.

00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:30.133
New episodes of "Severance"

00:04:30.133 --> 00:04:32.634
can be seen Fridays on Apple TV Plus.

